       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks like it may be an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850\u20131,000 mg per dose. At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max dose)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose you had in mind\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
